prompt:
Overhead flat-lay editorial photograph of a sunlit kitchen table in the morning, shot straight down. Pale natural oak tabletop, soft window light from the left with gentle leaf-shaped shadows. Three small arrangements sit in a single row from left to right with generous open space between them:
1) a clear vintage Edison light bulb with a brass base lying on a folded off-white linen napkin;
2) two halves of a red apple, cut side up, side by side: the left half has turned golden brown, the right half is fresh and creamy white with a halved lemon beside it and a few drops of juice on its surface;
3) a round slice of a tree trunk with clear concentric growth rings and a thin bark rim, used as a board, with a small ceramic cup of tea beside it.

Bright, airy, natural color, high-end lifestyle magazine photography, realistic textures, soft natural shadows, calm and uncluttered, lots of clean table surface. No people, no hands, no text, no labels, no logos, no packaging.
